# Vélu quotient by an odd cyclic kernel has nonzero discriminant

Theorem statement: `WeierstrassCurve.veluQuotient_oddOrderSummingSet_discriminant_ne_zero`
(`01bf34f6-bad2-52b8-83ef-b795fb714c92`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `8e008aec-90e8-5c2d-8f8e-e9c0a48d278c`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field in which $2 \neq 0$, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over
$L$ which is elliptic (its discriminant is a unit), let $n$ be a natural number, and let $Q$ be a
point of the associated affine curve whose additive order is exactly $2n+1$. Let $S$ be the finite
subset of $L \times L$ obtained as the image of $\{1,\dots,n\}$ under $k \mapsto$ the coordinate
pair of $k \cdot Q$, where a point $(x,y)$ is sent to $(x,y)$ and the point at infinity is sent to
$(0,0)$; thus $S$ records the affine coordinates of $Q, 2Q, \dots, nQ$, one representative of each
pair $\{kQ,-kQ\}$ of nonzero elements of $\langle Q \rangle$. Let $t = \sum_{P \in S}
\mathrm{veluT}(P)$ and $w = \sum_{P \in S} \mathrm{veluW}(P)$ be the corresponding Vélu sums, and
let $W'$ be the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $W$ and with $a_4' = a_4 - 5t$,
$a_6' = a_6 - b_2 t - 7w$. The assertion is that the discriminant of $W'$ is nonzero, i.e.
$\Delta(W') \neq 0$.

This is the statement that Vélu's formulas for the quotient of an elliptic curve by the cyclic
subgroup generated by a point of odd order again produce an elliptic curve, in the form "the target
has nonzero discriminant" over an algebraically closed field of characteristic different from $2$.
It is used in the treatment of modular polynomials and $\Gamma_0(N)$-moduli points, where the
assignment of a curve to its Vélu quotient must land among elliptic curves, notably in the results
on roots of the modular polynomial specialised at a transcendental $j$-invariant and in the
separability statement for such specialisations.

